    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0523" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/27.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Page.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose a copy of a letter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d621-f1"/> from Mr. Redfield, Secretary of Commerce, communicating a
                    copy of one received by him from the <pb facs="0524" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/>
                    Bishop of Long Island regarding the Reverend Dominic Cassetta, a clergyman of
                    Long Island, who, on his return to Italy on a visit, has been held to serve in
                    the Italian Army.</p>
                <p>In view of the fact that Mr. Cassetta came to the United States when of very
                    tender years, that his father became a naturalized citizen, that Mr. Cassetta
                    visited Italy for purposes of study, and in view of his religious calling, the
                    Department thinks that you may make a special appeal to the Italian Government
                    in his behalf, stating that this Government would much appreciate action on the
                    part of the Italian authorities permitting Mr. Cassetta to return to the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
